    "seconds": 182,
    "summary": "The `adFailure` feature flag was set to `on` by default, and I changed it back to `off`. The cause is a config drift from the upstream demo, not a crash loop: every pod was Running before my change.\n\n**What I found**\n- The `flagd-config` ConfigMap had `adFailure` with `\"defaultVariant\": \"on\"`. Upstream uses `off`. That flag makes the ad service fail requests, so the shop's ad feature would break for every request.\n- `ad` and `flagd` were both restarted at <time>, so they picked up the change together.\n- Ad logs from the last 10 minutes showed no errors, so I did not observe the failure directly. The frontend \"UNAVAILABLE\" errors are from before ad was ready.\n\n**What I changed**\n- Set `adFailure.defaultVariant` to `off` in `flagd-config` and applied it. This was the only edit to the file; I confirmed no other `\"defaultVariant\": \"on\"` existed.\n- Restarted `flagd`, because its init container copies the config only at pod start. The rollout succeeded.\n\n**Verification**\n- The live `/app/data/demo.flagd.json` in the flagd pod now shows `adFailure` `defaultVariant` as `off`.\n- All pods in `astronomy-shop` are Running.\n- An OFREP check to flagd timed out. I think the Service doesn't expose that port, but I did not confirm it, so this is untested.\n\nI did not change the `ad` deployment, and I did not check the shop end to end through the frontend.",
    "timed_out": false,
    "turns": 15,
